      "interleaving": "The topic's handlers are [A, B, C]. Thread 1 starts publish() and invokes A; the list iterator is now positioned for B. During A's callback, Thread 2 calls unsubscribe(topic, B), changing the list to [A, C]. Thread 1 resumes and its next iterator step yields C, so B is skipped. Python list iteration does not raise RuntimeError here; the bug is the unstable live-iteration behavior."
    }
  ]
}
